    "result": "{\"analysis\":\"All four proposals last round were refused only because the rationale gave the best KL rounded to 0.436144, which does not appear in any record. This round I quote numbers only as they appear in the records.\\n\\nThere is almost no room in the budget. The current best (avg_bits 3.147953869047619) sits just under budget_bits 403/128. Moving an MLP layer up one bit costs about 3.1M bits, so every upgrade needs a matching downgrade. The only per-layer KL rows retrieved are for layers that already sit high on the loss list, so I can't find a cheap layer to downgrade. Within the same bit width, the current methods are already the best choice for each retrieved layer.\\n\\nThat leaves GPTQ option changes, which cost no bits: act_order, damp and block_size. I apply each to every GPTQ-family method in use and leave the per-layer methods unchanged.\",\"stop\":false,\"proposals\":[{\"name\":\"opt_act_order_v2\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true}},\"rationale\":\"No bits change. Outlier activation channels drive the loss: layer 27 up_proj has activation kurtosis 1090.09 [E24beed188b6a] and loses 0.0057182 under gptq_int3 [Ef04d8aa7bded]. Setting act_order=true quantizes the high-Hessian columns first, which should lower GPTQ error on these layers.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E24beed188b6a\",\"Ef04d8aa7bded\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_damp_low_v2\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.005}},\"rationale\":\"No bits change. At 2 bits, layer 14 down_proj loses 0.00633466 under rht_gptq_int2 [E4c3f9b73e065]. A lower damp=0.005 makes GPTQ follow the calibration Hessian more closely, which may lower error on the low-bit layers.\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E4c3f9b73e065\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_damp_high_v2\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.damp\":0.05}},\"rationale\":\"No bits change. This is the opposite direction to damp=0.005: damp=0.05 regularizes the Hessians, which are dominated by outliers (activation kurtosis 1090.09 [E24beed188b6a]). That could reduce overfitting to the calibration set, since layer 27 gate_proj loses 0.00498703 under rht_gptq_int3 [Efa0bb391da67].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E24beed188b6a\",\"Efa0bb391da67\"]},{\"name\":\"opt_act_order_bs64\",\"base\":\"iso_3.15\",\"changes\":[],\"options\":{\"gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.block_size\":64},\"gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.block_size\":64},\"gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.block_size\":64},\"rht_gptq_int2\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.block_size\":64},\"rht_gptq_int3\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.block_size\":64},\"rht_gptq_int4\":{\"weight_algo.act_order\":true,\"weight_algo.block_size\":64}},\"rationale\":\"No bits change. This combines act_order=true with block_size=64 for the MLP layers where the loss concentrates, such as layer 3 up_proj, which loses 0.0064177 under rht_gptq_int3 [E6f4f7ea296d5].\",\"cites\":[\"E514ab09c524e\",\"E6f4f7ea296d5\"]}]}",
